                    <death when="1796-07-23"/>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Godwin called on a J Cooper on 19 March 1796 and then 
     recorded his death on 23 July. </p>
                        <p>There is a strong possibility that this is Jack Cooper, Thomas Cooper's younger brother. He is also mentioned in 1792.
      The entry for 3 January 1792 reads: <lb/>
      3. Tu. Talk with Marshal on sullenness : with J C on honesty and talents <lb/>
      and later in June that year: 
      5. Tu. Revise. Dyson calls, talk of force and the virtue of fools .
      Sup at miss Godwin's , talk of justice and speaking truth . J Cooper bound. <lb/>
      Godwin notes that J Cooper dies in  1796 .</p>
                    </note>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
